    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily on the combination of favorable park factors and aggressive platoon matchups to exploit the slate. **Brice Turang** (73.65) is our highest-rated play, buoyed by an ideal matchup against Kyle Freeland. The +14% park factor and the 90% stolen base opportunity window against Freeland\u2019s slow delivery make him the engine of our roster today. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** (71.43) remains an elite start against Cade Cavalli, benefiting from a +6% platoon edge and a prime #2 slot in the order that maximizes his chances to score runs. While **Josh Naylor** (67.19) and **Jose Caballero** (63.66) lack the same ceiling, they provide solid, high-floor value; specifically, **Jose Caballero** gains significant value from a +13% platoon edge and wind conditions playing in his favor, making him a high-efficiency play despite the lower-order projection.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **Austin Riley**, who yielded a score of 43.23. While his talent is clear, he was bypassed primarily due to a 19% downgrade against the skill of Mason Montgomery, which pushed his efficiency below the threshold required to crack our starting nine. We also continue to monitor **Seiya Suzuki**, who narrowly missed the cut at 42.34 due to a headwind warning and unfavorable matchup metrics. Our primary risks today revolve around the high number of \"Lineup Pending\" tags, particularly for **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Kyle Karros**, **James Wood**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino**. Should official lineups shift these players into lower-order roles, their efficiency scores will see immediate downward pressure. Furthermore, **Travis Bazzana** faces a daunting task against Jacob deGrom; while his #1 spot in the order provides a floor, the 19% SP skill penalty necessitates a careful watch on early-game outcomes for the rest of our bench, including **Mickey Moniak**, who remains unavailable on the IL alongside stashed depth pieces like **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Henry Bolte**.",
